<services>
  <!-- Source delivery for the OBS package (home:milnet:ants-terminal).

       obs_scm runs SERVER-SIDE (no mode attribute): the OBS servers have
       network, so they clone the pinned tag themselves and store a source
       archive (.obscpio + .obsinfo). tar / recompress then run at BUILD TIME
       inside the VM, off that archive.

       Why buildtime and not mode="manual": `tar` does not exist as a
       server-side service — a plain server-side run fails with
       "400 remote error: /usr/lib/obs/service//tar.service No such file or
       directory". mode="manual" (what finbreak uses) is the other way to avoid
       that, but it requires a local `osc service manualrun` and committing a
       ~7.5 MB tarball on every release. mode="buildtime" needs neither: no
       large upload, and "Trigger Services" in the web UI is enough.

       There was a third buildtime service here, set_version (removed by
       ANTS-3731). The job it did is still load-bearing: ants-terminal.spec's
       Version: field tracks CMakeLists.txt, which under the RC cadence always
       names the NEXT (unreleased) version, so between /bump and the next
       promote the spec names a tag that does not exist and Source0 would 404.
       obs-submit.sh now stamps Version: from the <revision> below when it
       copies the spec — same single source of truth (the tag), computed at
       submit time instead of in the VM.

       Caveat on mode="buildtime" (OBS user guide, ch. Source Services): a
       buildtime service package becomes a BUILD DEPENDENCY of the job and must
       be available in the target repository. That is what forced the change —
       openSUSE:Tools cannot build obs-service-set_version for Mageia at all,
       so the whole job went unresolvable over one rewritten line. tar and
       recompress remain because they have no such gap in the targets we build;
       check the same thing when adding a distro, because the symptom is an
       unresolvable job rather than an obviously service-related error.

       To release a new version: bump <revision> to the new tag, commit, and run
       packaging/obs/obs-submit.sh (or click Trigger Services). -->
  <service name="obs_scm">
    <param name="scm">git</param>
    <param name="url">https://github.com/milnet01/ants-terminal.git</param>
    <param name="revision">v0.7.106</param>
    <param name="match-tag">v*</param>
    <param name="versionformat">@PARENT_TAG@</param>
    <param name="versionrewrite-pattern">v(.*)</param>
    <param name="versionrewrite-replacement">\1</param>
    <param name="filename">ants-terminal</param>
  </service>
  <!-- versionformat/versionrewrite above also name the tarball the tar service
       produces (ants-terminal-<version>.tar). obs-submit.sh stamps the spec's
       Version: with the same transform, so Source0 resolves. Change one and
       you must change the other. -->
  <service name="tar" mode="buildtime"/>
  <service name="recompress" mode="buildtime">
    <param name="file">ants-terminal-*.tar</param>
    <param name="compression">gz</param>
  </service>
</services>
